body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Add defensive guards when dereferencing and mapping properties from `assertions` and `ref` elements in `buildMeasuredCalibration` to ignore nullish or malformed elements, preventing potential `TypeError` exceptions.

```javascript
  const evidenceFamilies = assertions.flatMap((assertion) => (
    assertion && typeof assertion === 'object' && Array.isArray(assertion.evidence_refs)
      ? assertion.evidence_refs
      : []
  ));
  const distinctEvidenceFamiliesByStatus = {};
  for (const assertion of assertions) {
    if (!assertion || typeof assertion !== 'object') continue;
    const status = assertion.status_proposal ?? 'none';
    if (!distinctEvidenceFamiliesByStatus[status]) distinctEvidenceFamiliesByStatus[status] = new Set();
    const refs = Array.isArray(assertion.evidence_refs) ? assertion.evidence_refs : [];
    for (const ref of refs) {
      if (ref && typeof ref === 'object') {
        distinctEvidenceFamiliesByStatus[status].add(ref.source_family ?? 'none');
      }
    }
  }
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When filtering or mapping arrays of objects, use defensive guards (such as checking if the element is a valid object) to ignore nullish or malformed elements instead of throwing a TypeError.
</details>

