body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Add defensive guards when mapping and finding elements in `policyEntries` inside `buildValidatorResult` to ignore nullish or malformed elements, preventing potential `TypeError` exceptions.

```javascript
  const policyPredicates = sortedUnique(
    policyEntries
      .filter((entry) => entry && typeof entry === 'object')
      .map((entry) => entry.predicate)
  );
  const requiredPolicyPredicates = [
    ...SAFE_PREDICATES,
    'high_risk_prerequisite_misconception_mastery_edges',
  ].sort(compareByteOrder);
  const missingPolicyPredicates = requiredPolicyPredicates.filter((predicate) => (
    !policyPredicates.includes(predicate)
  ));
  const highRiskEntry = policyEntries.find((entry) => entry && typeof entry === 'object' && entry.risk_tier === HIGH_RISK);
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When filtering or mapping arrays of objects, use defensive guards (such as checking if the element is a valid object) to ignore nullish or malformed elements instead of throwing a TypeError.
</details>

